.TH "ROARK\-LIVE\-REPORT\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-live-report-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-live\-report\-create \- Create a live report
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark live\-report create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Saves a report on the project's live calls. Simulations are never included. Targets are analytics measures held to a bar: a threshold metric is read as its pass rate (`value` is a percentage, 0\-100, held AT_LEAST by default); a numeric metric as its average (held AT_MOST by default). Every target is read for the period and the period before it, so the report says whether each was met and how it moved. Scheduled reports are written `deliveryHour` hours into the day after each period ends in `timezone` (a week runs Monday to Sunday), then emailed and posted per `notifications`. With `generateNow` (the default) the report for the latest closed period is written right away and not sent.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/live\-report
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
